# Chromeleon Overlay Architecture

## 🎯 Core Architecture Principle

**Chromeleon is a single-page app that overlays and completely replaces the user experience of visited webpages.**

## 🏗️ Architectural Requirements

### Host Page (Original Website)
- **MUST remain completely unmodified**
- **ONLY exception**: Scroll prevention (`overflow-hidden` class)
- **NO CSS changes** to original page elements
- **NO DOM injection** into original page

### Overlay System
- **Shadow DOM isolation** - all content in shadow DOM
- **React component rendering** - all UI built with React
- **Complete user experience replacement** - users interact with overlay, not original page
- **Theme-governed styling** - selected UI library (shadcn/daisy) controls appearance

### Data Flow
- **Page scraping** - extract content from original page to JSON
- **JSON interpretation** - React app processes scraped data
- **Component rendering** - React components display processed data
- **User interaction** - all interaction happens within overlay

## 🚫 Architectural Violations (NEVER ALLOWED)

### Host Page Modification
- **CSS injection into main document**
- **DOM manipulation of original page elements**
- **Style overrides on host page**
- **Adding elements to original page**

### Direct DOM Manipulation
- **Style property manipulation** (`element.style.*`)
- **CSS injection** (`style.textContent`, `createElement('style')`)
- **Inline styles** (`style="..."` or `style={{...}}`)
- **Direct HTML injection** (use React components instead)

## ✅ Required Architectural Patterns

### React-First Approach
- **React components** for all UI elements
- **JSX rendering** instead of HTML injection
- **Component state management** for dynamic behavior
- **Props and hooks** for data flow

### Shadow DOM Isolation
- **All overlay content** in shadow DOM
- **External CSS loading** via `<link>` elements only
- **Theme data attributes** on shadow DOM host
- **Class-based styling** with Tailwind/DaisyUI

### Data Processing Pipeline
- **Content scraping** → JSON conversion
- **JSON processing** → React component props
- **Component rendering** → User interface
- **User interaction** → Overlay-only responses

## 🔧 Implementation Checklist

**Before implementing any feature:**
- [ ] Does this modify the original webpage? → **MUST BE NO**
- [ ] Is this contained within the overlay? → **MUST BE YES**
- [ ] Does this use React components? → **MUST BE YES**
- [ ] Does this follow shadow DOM isolation? → **MUST BE YES**
- [ ] Does this use proper CSS loading? → **MUST BE YES**

## 📋 Correct Implementation Examples

### ✅ Overlay Creation
```tsx
// Create shadow DOM overlay
const { host, shadow } = ensureShadowHost('chromeleon-root');
// Load CSS externally
const link = document.createElement('link');
link.href = chrome.runtime.getURL('src/styles/content.css');
shadow.appendChild(link);
```

### ✅ React Component Rendering
```tsx
// All UI in React components
function OverlayApp() {
  return (
    <div className="fixed inset-0 bg-base-100">
      <ChromeleonApp />
    </div>
  );
}
```

### ✅ Data Scraping & Rendering
```tsx
// Scrape page data to JSON
const pageData = scrapePageToJSON();
// Render with React components
<SchemaRenderer data={pageData} theme={selectedTheme} />
```

## 🎯 Architecture Summary

1. **Original page**: Unmodified, only scroll prevention
2. **Overlay**: Shadow DOM with React app
3. **Data**: Scraped to JSON, processed by React
4. **Styling**: External CSS + Tailwind/DaisyUI classes
5. **Interaction**: All within overlay, none with original page
